From: LukeValen <panvk-eden@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH csf-v11 106] panvk: disable kbase cross-subqueue GPU waits by default

Purpose: A captured Eden hang on Mali-G615 showed all three kbase CSF
subqueues parked at seqno 159 while waiting for target 163, with no kbase
error bit set. This is consistent with a userspace-generated circular
cross-subqueue wait. Keep semaphore waits on the CPU by default for the
dedicated Eden build until the GPU dependency path is proven deadlock-free.

Developers can re-enable the asynchronous path explicitly with:
PANVK_KBASE_GPU_SEMAPHORE_WAITS=1

Target: Eden Android / Mali-G615 MC6 / Kbase CSF v11

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_gpu_queue.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_gpu_queue.c
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_gpu_queue.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_gpu_queue.c
@@ -2677,10 +2677,17 @@ panvk_queue_submit_init_signals(struct panvk_queue_submit *submit,
 }
 
 #ifdef HAVE_PAN_KMOD_KBASE
-/* Enabled by default for async submission and full GPU utilization: */
-/* set PANVK_KBASE_GPU_SEMAPHORE_WAITS=0 to disable GPU waits. */
+/* Eden/Kbase stability default: keep cross-subqueue semaphore waits on the
+ * CPU until the userspace CSF dependency scheme is proven deadlock-free on
+ * the reference Mali-G615.  A captured Eden hang showed all three subqueues
+ * parked at seqno 159 while waiting for target 163, with no kbase error bit,
+ * which is consistent with a userspace-generated circular GPU wait.
+ *
+ * Developers can explicitly re-enable the asynchronous path with
+ * PANVK_KBASE_GPU_SEMAPHORE_WAITS=1 for isolated testing.
+ */
 DEBUG_GET_ONCE_BOOL_OPTION(kbase_gpu_semaphore_waits,
-                           "PANVK_KBASE_GPU_SEMAPHORE_WAITS", true)
+                           "PANVK_KBASE_GPU_SEMAPHORE_WAITS", false)
 
 static bool
 kbase_gpu_waits_disabled(void)
